# Storefront Agent — Scope

This project is a monorepo (`apps/server` = Vendure backend, `apps/storefront` = Next.js 16). See root `AGENTS.md` for workspace commands.

## Boundaries

- Work only in `apps/storefront/` unless explicitly asked otherwise.
- Do not modify `apps/server/`. If a feature needs a new Shop API field, mutation, or plugin, describe what the backend must expose — do not implement backend changes or stub fake data.
- Minimize diff scope; no drive-by refactors.

## Git and secrets

- No commits unless the user asks.
- Never commit `.env` or hardcode secrets.
- Document new env vars in `.env.example` only when requested.

## Backend coordination

When backend support is required, state clearly: *"This requires a Vendure plugin / Shop API extension in `apps/server`"* and specify the GraphQL shape the storefront expects.

## Communication

- Cite existing code with file paths when explaining changes.
- Prefer extending existing components over parallel implementations.
- Ask before large architectural shifts (new state library, replacing `gql.tada`, app router restructure).
